  "notes": "{振|ふ}るう means to wield or exercise something with active force — whether a physical tool or an abstract power.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{振|ふ}るう: to wield ~, to exercise ~\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {腕|うで}を{振|ふ}るう: to display one's skill (literally \"wield one's arm\")\n- {暴力|ぼうりょく}を{振|ふ}るう: to resort to violence\n- {権力|けんりょく}を{振|ふ}るう: to wield power\n- {手腕|しゅわん}を{振|ふ}るう: to demonstrate one's abilities\n- {包丁|ほうちょう}を{振|ふ}るう: to wield a kitchen knife (i.e., to cook)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {振|ふ}るう (to wield) vs {奮|ふる}う (to rouse oneself, to muster) — different kanji, different meanings\n- {振|ふ}るう (to wield) vs {震|ふる}える (to tremble) — different words entirely",
